      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of books in the warehouse.\n2. Determine how many new boxes Melvin can pack with 40 books each.\n3. Find out how many books are left over after repacking.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the total number of books:\n\\[\n1335 \\text{ boxes} \\times 39 \\text{ books per box} = 52165 \\text{ books}\n\\]\n\nNext, determine how many new boxes Melvin can pack with 40 books each:\n\\[\n\\left\\lfloor \\frac{52165}{40} \\right\\rfloor = 1304 \\text{ boxes}\n\\]\n\nNow, calculate the total number of books that can be packed in these 1304 boxes:\n\\[\n1304 \\text{ boxes} \\times 40 \\text{ books per box} = 52160 \\text{ books}\n\\]\n\nFinally, to find the number of books left over, subtract the number of books packed from the total number of books:\n\\[\n52165 \\text{ books} - 52160 \\text{ books} = 5 \\text{ books}\n\\]\n\nSo the number of books left over after repacking is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{5}\n\\]",
